WEBVTT

00:01.240 --> 00:02.640
[clattering]

00:03.520 --> 00:05.000
[fluttering]

00:13.360 --> 00:15.160
[indistinct shouting]

00:18.440 --> 00:20.080
[clamoring]

00:29.400 --> 00:32.360
[Arthur] All right...
First come, first served.

00:32.439 --> 00:35.240
Form an orderly line, all of you.

00:35.320 --> 00:37.520
All right. All right. [sniffs]

00:39.000 --> 00:43.280
Right. Have your contracts
of employment in your hand.

00:43.360 --> 00:46.280
Bring 'em in. Get in there...

00:46.360 --> 00:50.640
Get moving... On you go... Go on...
Keep going... Keep going.

00:50.720 --> 00:53.560
-You, where are you going?
-Bradley. Foreman.

00:53.640 --> 00:56.920
All right. You go and see
that man over there. Go!

00:58.960 --> 01:01.160
-What's your name?
-Bradley. I'm the foreman.

01:01.240 --> 01:03.000
-When did you last work here?
-1922.

01:03.560 --> 01:05.360
How many have done
this type of work before?

01:05.440 --> 01:07.160
They're mostly farm hands
from down Worcester way.

01:07.240 --> 01:09.280
But I'll show 'em.
Hungry men learn fast.

01:09.360 --> 01:11.040
All right. On you go.

01:11.160 --> 01:13.880
[man] Dirty scabs! Black legs!

01:13.960 --> 01:15.880
-[clamoring continues]
-[shattering]

01:15.960 --> 01:19.560
What bastard threw that?
Get him out here.

01:20.440 --> 01:21.720
Bring him out!

01:21.800 --> 01:23.200
[indistinct shouting]

01:24.320 --> 01:25.800
[grunts]

01:29.640 --> 01:32.280
Arthur! Oi! Enough. Enough.

01:32.360 --> 01:36.040
Get him out. Get out!
All right, 10 more.

01:39.760 --> 01:41.880
Two more. That's it.

01:41.960 --> 01:43.560
-Ten.
-Close it up!

01:49.640 --> 01:53.720
Right. Ten bob a man.
Two pound there for you.

01:53.800 --> 01:54.880
What about security?

01:54.960 --> 01:56.240
Yeah, well, about that.

01:56.320 --> 01:59.200
By order of the City of Birmingham
Police Department,

01:59.280 --> 02:04.200
you and your ugly workforce
are now under the protection

02:04.280 --> 02:06.520
of the Peaky Fucking Blinders.

02:17.560 --> 02:18.920
[footsteps approaching]

02:19.920 --> 02:21.080
[door opens]

02:22.760 --> 02:25.160
-Mr. Gray?
-[Michael] Yeah, send him in.

02:25.240 --> 02:26.440
It's your mother.

02:26.520 --> 02:29.120
Oh, fuck...

02:40.200 --> 02:42.320
I read about it in the paper.

02:44.560 --> 02:46.120
I have a right.

02:48.720 --> 02:50.440
I'm your mom as well.

02:56.520 --> 02:58.040
You want me to go away?

02:59.640 --> 03:01.080
Yes.

03:04.280 --> 03:05.800
I'll just leave these.

03:11.400 --> 03:12.960
They're from our orchard.

03:19.880 --> 03:21.280
You used to love these.

03:22.760 --> 03:24.800
-I hope there are no worms in 'em.
-[chuckles]

03:31.600 --> 03:33.120
[sighs]

03:49.840 --> 03:51.880
Look,

03:51.960 --> 03:54.440
I just wanted to say
that you're welcome to come home.

03:56.320 --> 04:00.760
To get better at home.
I know you got bored in the village...

04:02.720 --> 04:03.960
But we love you

04:05.200 --> 04:08.480
and your little brother
misses playing football with you.

04:09.960 --> 04:11.400
And your dad...

04:13.560 --> 04:15.160
Passed on.

04:17.079 --> 04:19.240
He passed on peacefully in our bed.

04:19.680 --> 04:20.720
[exhales]

04:22.800 --> 04:23.840
Fuck...

04:30.000 --> 04:32.120
Now, go on.

04:32.200 --> 04:35.840
I'm expecting Tommy,
and he is due here now.

04:38.000 --> 04:39.440
I'll go then.

04:41.520 --> 04:44.160
I'll not be in the same room
as that man.

04:58.960 --> 05:02.280
[door opens and closes]

05:11.000 --> 05:12.400
[vehicle approaching]

05:29.000 --> 05:30.200
[door opens]

05:30.280 --> 05:32.560
Come on, Pol, Tommy’s expecting us.

05:34.280 --> 05:38.000
-Who's with us?
-Isiah and two Lee boys.

05:39.880 --> 05:43.160
Ada? How long since you've had a fuck?

05:44.320 --> 05:47.640
-What?
-It's been nearly two years with me.

05:48.720 --> 05:51.120
Over Christmas, I counted it up.

05:51.200 --> 05:54.560
So I've made a New Year's resolution
to change the situation.

05:54.640 --> 05:58.120
Oh, anyone particular in mind?

05:58.200 --> 06:00.520
Not really.

06:00.600 --> 06:03.640
Just me and someone unsuitable.

06:18.280 --> 06:19.720
I'll sit in the front.

06:42.720 --> 06:45.200
So, this is just
to make things official.

06:45.280 --> 06:47.520
Your official return
to the company payroll.

06:47.600 --> 06:48.600
So no more talk

06:48.680 --> 06:51.200
of New Year's resolutions
or Tommy might change his mind.

06:51.280 --> 06:53.160
What New Year's resolution?

06:53.240 --> 06:54.440
Never mind.

06:56.440 --> 06:58.720
I think Ada's trying to tell me
to behave myself.

06:58.840 --> 07:01.040
Yeah. Behave yourself.

07:02.040 --> 07:03.920
Behave myself or what?

07:05.200 --> 07:07.520
Behave myself or fucking what?

07:09.120 --> 07:11.560
Okay, Polly, I'll tell you the truth.

07:11.640 --> 07:14.560
After your recent troubles,
Tommy asked me to keep an eye on you.

07:14.640 --> 07:16.160
Troubles?

07:17.120 --> 07:19.160
Whilst working for this company,

07:19.240 --> 07:22.040
I have killed a man,
I have lost a man,

07:22.120 --> 07:24.280
I have found a son,
I have nearly lost a son,

07:24.360 --> 07:26.480
I have nearly lost my own life.

07:27.640 --> 07:33.800
Now I will accept my job back
if the terms on offer are favorable.

07:36.360 --> 07:38.560
But I will not behave myself.

07:48.040 --> 07:49.320
[footsteps approaching]

07:49.680 --> 07:50.760
[door opens]

07:51.880 --> 07:53.320
Sorry I'm late.

08:02.920 --> 08:04.400
Where's Arthur?

08:06.560 --> 08:08.560
Do I look like his fucking mother?

08:23.400 --> 08:24.400
Oh, Linda...

08:25.680 --> 08:27.200
Why are you here?

08:27.280 --> 08:29.040
You all right? Is Billy all right?

08:29.120 --> 08:31.320
Yes. Everything's fine.

08:31.400 --> 08:34.200
Well, look. Lovely to see you.
But I'm late for a meeting.

08:34.320 --> 08:35.880
They can wait.

08:43.240 --> 08:44.920
I've got something for you.

08:45.680 --> 08:48.160
Something for a loving husband
who's been working very hard...

08:49.400 --> 08:52.200
And is under a great deal of pressure.

08:55.440 --> 08:58.720
Something to relieve his stress.

08:59.480 --> 09:00.640
Oh.

09:07.200 --> 09:11.880
It's silk. From Japan. Feel.

09:17.480 --> 09:19.880
-My hands are dirty.
-Good.

09:20.920 --> 09:22.080
Feel all of it.

09:24.360 --> 09:25.680
Feel it properly.

09:26.240 --> 09:27.680
[both breathing heavily]

09:33.680 --> 09:37.320
You, uh... You want to do this here?

09:38.280 --> 09:40.960
Why not? I thought you were the boss.

09:42.000 --> 09:43.680
I am the fucking boss.

09:43.760 --> 09:45.680
Then tell me what to do, boss.

09:47.880 --> 09:49.240
Come here.

09:50.120 --> 09:54.400
[Tommy] Right, before we start
this extraordinary general meeting

09:54.480 --> 09:57.200
of the board of the
Shelby Company Limited,

09:57.280 --> 10:00.520
I'd like to note the absence
of the Deputy Vice President

10:00.600 --> 10:02.360
who has not yet arrived.

10:02.480 --> 10:04.640
We will continue without his presence.

10:04.720 --> 10:08.240
[clears throat] Item number one,
the reinstatement

10:10.120 --> 10:12.600
of the Shelby Company Limited
company treasurer.

10:12.720 --> 10:14.440
The board welcomes back

10:14.520 --> 10:15.960
the former treasurer,

10:16.040 --> 10:18.280
with generously improved
terms and conditions.

10:18.360 --> 10:19.800
Due to the exceptionally

10:19.880 --> 10:21.280
difficult circumstances

10:21.360 --> 10:23.120
the company now finds itself in.

10:23.200 --> 10:25.880
The proposed treasurer will now
check the terms and conditions

10:25.960 --> 10:27.680
to see if they are in order.

10:29.240 --> 10:33.360
Item number two, during the absence
of the company accountant

10:33.440 --> 10:34.840
due to ill health,

10:34.920 --> 10:37.200
all responsibility for
the keeping of company accounts

10:37.280 --> 10:40.320
pass to the head of acquisitions.

10:41.960 --> 10:44.000
Item number three.

10:44.080 --> 10:46.960
The company treasurer,
having read the terms and condition,

10:47.040 --> 10:48.760
lodges a signed contract of employment

10:48.840 --> 10:52.440
agreeing to the terms and conditions
with the temporary head of accounts.

10:52.520 --> 10:56.000
All those in favor of the
reinstatement of Mrs. Elizabeth Gray,

10:56.080 --> 10:57.120
to the position of

10:57.200 --> 10:59.320
Shelby Company Limited
Company Treasurer,

10:59.400 --> 11:00.440
please raise your hands.

11:02.000 --> 11:03.480
Why, goodness. Thank you.

11:03.600 --> 11:05.200
Any other business?

11:05.400 --> 11:09.840
Right, I declare this
extraordinary general meeting over.

11:11.040 --> 11:12.760
Now we can talk about
the real business.

11:14.160 --> 11:15.760
But for that, we need Arthur.

11:16.480 --> 11:18.280
Where the fuck is Arthur?

11:20.040 --> 11:21.280
[moaning]

11:39.920 --> 11:41.000
[knocking on door]

11:41.360 --> 11:43.680
-[Devlin] Mr. Shelby...
-Fuck off.

11:43.760 --> 11:45.280
They’ve broken into the paint shop.

11:45.360 --> 11:46.360
Oh, yeah?

11:46.440 --> 11:47.760
They’re chucking paint around,

11:47.840 --> 11:49.760
I think they mean to set light to it.

11:49.840 --> 11:53.840
Well, you deal with it, man.
I’m fucking busy!

11:54.200 --> 11:55.680
[moaning]

11:58.280 --> 11:59.320
[grunts]

12:18.880 --> 12:20.560
What was all that about?

12:23.680 --> 12:24.880
[breathes heavily]

12:36.800 --> 12:41.600
In this sinful place
there will be temptations.

12:41.680 --> 12:46.320
It’s my responsibility as your wife
to help you resist those temptations.

12:47.800 --> 12:50.000
By putting myself between you...

12:55.400 --> 12:56.760
And the devil.

12:58.880 --> 13:00.800
In the words of
my sinful Catholic mother,

13:01.760 --> 13:04.760
"Keep his balls empty
and his belly full."

13:06.440 --> 13:08.680
-God rest her soul.
-[chuckles]

13:09.360 --> 13:10.480
[knock on door]

13:10.560 --> 13:11.880
[Devlin] Mr. Shelby...

13:11.960 --> 13:15.280
You have to come to the paint shop
immediately! Please!

13:19.760 --> 13:21.320
Oh, I have to go.

13:22.200 --> 13:24.040
Won't be late.

13:27.240 --> 13:28.360
[door opens]

13:28.960 --> 13:31.480
Sorry, ladies,
there's no smoking in here.

13:31.560 --> 13:33.000
Yes, love, we know.

13:35.560 --> 13:37.920
All right. He's an hour late.
Fuck him.

13:38.600 --> 13:42.000
[sighs] This business
directly affects Arthur,

13:42.080 --> 13:44.760
but he's not here,
so we'll take a vote without him.

13:45.240 --> 13:47.360
What business?

13:47.480 --> 13:50.160
Official business that wasn't
on your agenda, Ada.

13:50.440 --> 13:53.720
[Tommy] An informant told us
that six years ago,

13:53.800 --> 13:55.120
Luca Changretta

13:55.200 --> 13:56.600
came from New York to Birmingham

13:56.680 --> 13:58.520
to be best man
at his cousin's wedding.

13:58.600 --> 14:01.200
[Polly] We found out that they used
Reid and Dunn on Broadgate

14:01.280 --> 14:02.520
for the photographs.

14:02.640 --> 14:07.040
The photographer kept the negatives.
I persuaded him to give us copies.

14:07.160 --> 14:08.960
And to enlarge this one...

14:10.720 --> 14:13.920
That is Luca Changretta.

14:14.000 --> 14:16.600
[Tommy] I've seen his face,
so I could pick him out.

14:16.680 --> 14:19.280
Half the men in the photograph
are Changrettas,

14:19.360 --> 14:20.960
which means, chances are

14:21.040 --> 14:22.840
they are the men
who will come to kill us.

14:22.920 --> 14:26.560
We need to get both these photographs
into pubs and on street corners.

14:26.640 --> 14:29.560
Then we put it about that
there's a reward for information.

14:32.640 --> 14:36.080
We also propose that we give
a copy of this photograph

14:36.160 --> 14:37.560
to Mr. Aberama Gold.

14:38.280 --> 14:42.880
We need to forget the idea that it has
to be Arthur that pulls the trigger.

14:42.960 --> 14:45.480
Tradition will just fuck us up.

14:45.600 --> 14:49.120
-We should wait for Arthur...
-Arthur's not here, Ada.

14:49.200 --> 14:52.520
We need Luca Changretta dead.
That's it.

14:53.160 --> 14:54.440
[Polly] Dropping the law
of the bullet

14:54.520 --> 14:56.080
is part of the process
of modernization

14:56.160 --> 14:57.920
that I was working on before I...

14:58.920 --> 15:00.400
Before I was executed.

15:01.040 --> 15:04.880
-You weren't executed, Pol.
-What did you call me?

15:05.440 --> 15:07.640
[Tommy] Right. Let's take a vote.
I'll deal with Arthur.

15:07.720 --> 15:11.080
All those in favor
of giving the photographs to Mr. Gold,

15:11.160 --> 15:12.520
raise your hand.

15:24.440 --> 15:25.680
Then it will be done.

15:26.760 --> 15:29.040
-Mom...
-Oh, "Mom" now, is it?

15:30.400 --> 15:32.200
I smelt perfume when I came in here.

15:32.320 --> 15:33.840
Yeah, it was the flowers.

15:35.280 --> 15:38.240
-Right, that's it.
-Who came in here, Michael?

15:38.360 --> 15:41.760
The truth is, Polly, the woman
that raised him came in here.

15:41.840 --> 15:43.360
She has every right to come in here.

15:43.440 --> 15:45.560
She brought him fucking apples
and she left.

15:45.640 --> 15:48.640
We are in the middle of a vendetta
and Arthur is missing.

15:48.720 --> 15:50.120
We need to find him.

15:50.200 --> 15:52.560
Concentrate on what unites us.

15:52.680 --> 15:55.840
-This is all temporary.
-Yeah, temporary, right.

15:56.960 --> 15:57.960
[sighs heavily]

16:11.800 --> 16:13.160
[man] Bastards!

16:14.400 --> 16:15.920
[indistinct shouting]

16:33.840 --> 16:36.960
Party is it? Is that what it is?

16:37.040 --> 16:41.800
What is this, a party?
Fuck off out of it! Get out!

16:47.560 --> 16:50.640
Okay, I wasn't gonna hit ya.

16:50.720 --> 16:52.480
But that wasn't fucking nice.

16:52.720 --> 16:54.000
[both grunting]

16:57.640 --> 16:58.920
Oh, you...

17:03.240 --> 17:05.440
[man] Arthur, Mr. Shelby.
Please. Please!

17:05.520 --> 17:07.839
Don’t fucking move...

17:08.520 --> 17:09.960
Sorry, Mr. Shelby, please, please!

17:10.040 --> 17:11.640
Then get the fuck out!

17:13.960 --> 17:16.040
Fuck your fucking revolution.

17:26.319 --> 17:28.079
I am a fucking mess.

18:01.280 --> 18:02.280
Shh.

18:13.760 --> 18:15.000
[indistinct talking]

18:33.920 --> 18:34.960
[indistinct shouting]

18:54.680 --> 18:57.280
Where are you going? Come here...

18:57.360 --> 18:59.960
Fucking hit men, are you? Huh?

19:00.040 --> 19:01.480
Is that what you are?

19:03.040 --> 19:04.800
Arthur Shelby?

19:04.880 --> 19:06.440
That's who you wanted, yeah?

19:07.920 --> 19:09.280
What about...

19:09.360 --> 19:13.640
-What about fucking John Shelby?
-[man panting]

19:19.360 --> 19:20.480
[grunts]

19:36.680 --> 19:37.960
[breathes heavily]

19:40.400 --> 19:41.800
John.

20:25.760 --> 20:26.760
Thank you.

20:28.360 --> 20:29.960
Send my guests in.

20:33.440 --> 20:34.720
[door opens]

20:46.200 --> 20:47.200
[in Italian]

20:47.440 --> 20:49.920
They didn't come back

20:52.440 --> 20:55.600
Arthur Shelby is still alive

21:02.960 --> 21:06.000
Wire his village and tell them

21:13.160 --> 21:14.360
[speaking English]

21:14.440 --> 21:17.720
You wire Polo
and let him tell the family.

21:20.520 --> 21:23.520
He has four kids. [grunts]

21:31.080 --> 21:33.600
Don't you two have
any other clothes to wear?

21:34.240 --> 21:35.240
[in Italian]

21:35.480 --> 21:42.360
You walk around this little place
dressed like big city hoodlums

21:42.640 --> 21:43.720
[in English]

21:43.800 --> 21:45.160
Now look at me.

21:45.600 --> 21:46.600
Huh?

21:47.200 --> 21:49.600
I'm here as a lover of theater.

21:51.280 --> 21:52.280
[in Italian]

21:52.680 --> 21:56.440
None of my clothes fit anymore

21:56.520 --> 21:59.880
I can't eat anything, it's all shit

22:00.040 --> 22:02.360
It's inedible, it's disgusting!

22:02.760 --> 22:05.720
Spotted Dick? What is that?

22:05.920 --> 22:08.520
I don't want to eat that, why would I?

22:14.160 --> 22:17.120
[Luca sighs] They killed two of our men.

22:20.960 --> 22:22.880
You complain about your fucking belly.

22:26.480 --> 22:27.480
Luca...

22:27.800 --> 22:28.880
[speaks in Italian]

22:29.160 --> 22:31.720
Luca, with respect.

22:32.840 --> 22:35.440
-With respect.
-With respect?

22:35.520 --> 22:36.960
You raised...

22:39.560 --> 22:40.800
With respect?

22:42.480 --> 22:44.080
You open your mouth.

22:44.880 --> 22:47.360
-Come on...
-Open your fucking mouth.

22:48.760 --> 22:51.000
You fucking dress like them.

22:51.080 --> 22:52.920
You eat like them.

22:53.000 --> 22:55.760
You don't fucking talk to me
about, "With respect!"

22:56.000 --> 22:57.000
[muffled grunting]

22:57.080 --> 22:58.080
[in Italian]

22:58.280 --> 23:00.760
Let's get this business finished

23:00.840 --> 23:03.360
then we can all go home

23:04.960 --> 23:09.320
Then we can eat some decent food

23:15.960 --> 23:16.960
Sit down.

23:26.760 --> 23:27.760
What do you have?

23:27.840 --> 23:28.840
[in Italian]

23:29.040 --> 23:30.320
We found another enemy

23:31.720 --> 23:34.320
This family has lots of enemies

23:34.800 --> 23:35.800
[Matteo speaks in Italian]

23:36.080 --> 23:37.760
She lives inside their territory

23:38.880 --> 23:41.320
Arthur Shelby killed her son
in a boxing ring four years ago.

23:41.400 --> 23:42.400
[in Italian]

23:42.480 --> 23:45.760
She says he's crazy in the head

23:46.560 --> 23:49.160
To compensate her, they look
after her and her other kids

23:50.240 --> 23:53.080
She thinks if she asks one of
the brothers to come to her house

23:53.480 --> 23:55.280
they would come.

23:57.640 --> 23:59.440
-She would do that for us?
-[Frederico speaks Italian]

23:59.520 --> 24:00.560
So she says

24:01.640 --> 24:04.080
People in this place hate forever

24:04.760 --> 24:05.800
Like Sicilians

24:10.400 --> 24:11.400
Okay.

24:12.000 --> 24:13.200
Okay.

24:23.240 --> 24:24.760
[men talking indistinctly]

24:40.160 --> 24:41.640
[Tommy] Anyone seen Arthur?

24:44.600 --> 24:46.720
Anyone seen Arthur, eh?

24:46.800 --> 24:48.120
In your office, Tom.

24:55.120 --> 24:57.000
If you're not gonna show up
for a family meeting,

24:57.080 --> 24:58.320
you let someone know.

24:58.400 --> 25:01.760
We thought you were dead,
there's 15 fucking Italians out there.

25:01.840 --> 25:03.520
No, there's not.

25:03.600 --> 25:05.080
There's 13.

25:05.800 --> 25:07.200
I just killed two of them.

25:08.360 --> 25:11.680
Ripped out their hearts
and burnt their bones to ash.

25:12.680 --> 25:13.800
[sighs]

25:15.240 --> 25:16.240
Oh, I did it.

25:17.280 --> 25:19.040
Me.

25:19.120 --> 25:20.880
Your brother.

25:20.960 --> 25:25.240
Not fucking Aberama Gold
or his punch drunk son, but me!

25:27.680 --> 25:30.080
Even if you don't trust me no more.

25:30.960 --> 25:33.120
What the fuck are you talking about?
Arthur?

25:34.440 --> 25:35.960
I got cleaned up at Ada's.

25:37.520 --> 25:40.840
She told me
you took a vote in my absence.

25:40.920 --> 25:43.600
All right. Calm down,
and tell me about the men...

25:43.680 --> 25:46.600
You put my job out for contract.

25:46.680 --> 25:47.680
Arthur...

25:48.920 --> 25:51.280
Yeah, well, I'm gonna make it
my fucking job anyway.

25:51.680 --> 25:53.360
Because this was all my fault.

25:54.240 --> 25:56.320
It was me that shot the old man.

25:56.400 --> 25:57.840
-Yeah, out of mercy.
-Aye.

25:59.040 --> 26:01.080
Now John's dead,

26:01.160 --> 26:04.440
he's dead because of me
and I wanna make it right.

26:05.400 --> 26:06.400
Arthur, wait.

26:08.280 --> 26:10.560
How did the men get in the factory?
I need to know.

26:15.000 --> 26:17.000
Through the back fucking door

26:17.920 --> 26:21.560
that was supposed
to be locked and bolted.

26:21.720 --> 26:25.320
Some bastard gave me up.
Somebody with keys.

26:26.800 --> 26:30.680
Yeah. Why don't you sit down,
work it out for yourself?

26:33.320 --> 26:34.960
Take a fucking vote.

26:52.000 --> 26:53.840
Who's this little bear?

26:53.920 --> 26:55.160
Yes.

26:59.880 --> 27:01.080
You all right?

27:05.360 --> 27:06.520
Daddy's home.

27:08.320 --> 27:09.840
Yeah, I'm all right.

27:09.920 --> 27:11.640
Look, Daddy's home.

27:13.800 --> 27:15.040
How's Polly?

27:17.320 --> 27:18.320
She all right?

27:22.600 --> 27:24.040
Oh, go on, Linda.

27:25.680 --> 27:29.040
I mean, it was her idea, wasn’t it?
Hmm?

27:29.640 --> 27:31.120
The Japanese silk?

27:32.360 --> 27:34.080
I'll put him to bed.

27:40.200 --> 27:41.320
[door opens]

27:44.800 --> 27:46.840
You kept me away
from that fucking meeting

27:48.160 --> 27:50.800
-to stop me from voting.
-[Linda] Here we go.

27:50.880 --> 27:53.080
-[Arthur] Polly’s idea, wasn't it?
-[baby fussing]

27:53.320 --> 27:54.400
Eh?

27:55.520 --> 27:57.400
-You know what I am, don’t you?
-Shh, shh.

27:58.040 --> 27:59.560
I'm a working man.

28:00.560 --> 28:01.560
Yeah.

28:03.400 --> 28:04.920
Fucking working man.

28:06.880 --> 28:08.640
Fucking...

28:08.720 --> 28:10.040
Who's lost his job.

28:14.400 --> 28:17.800
Is that what I am, Linda?
Is that what I am, eh?

28:19.840 --> 28:22.040
-[door closes]
-[Linda] I don't want you dead.

28:22.680 --> 28:24.360
Polly doesn't want you dead.

28:24.640 --> 28:27.240
Let Mr. Gold do the killing.
For money.

28:28.040 --> 28:29.640
It's the modern way, Arthur.

28:33.280 --> 28:34.280
[Arthur] Watch.

28:36.840 --> 28:39.000
Hmm? Hmm?

28:46.520 --> 28:47.680
What are you doing?

28:50.000 --> 28:52.680
Now fire it into the fireplace.

28:53.760 --> 28:54.760
Please.

28:58.440 --> 29:00.200
-Fire it?
-Fire it.

29:02.640 --> 29:03.920
Get rid of it.

29:09.720 --> 29:11.160
Then we'll go to bed.

29:12.360 --> 29:13.880
Do anything you like.

29:15.240 --> 29:17.120
Just fire the gun, Arthur.

29:18.440 --> 29:19.440
Fire it.

29:20.080 --> 29:21.160
Ah!

29:21.840 --> 29:23.400
You go tell Polly...

29:26.160 --> 29:29.400
There are rules
between a man and a woman.

29:31.720 --> 29:32.840
Fucking rules.

29:39.120 --> 29:40.640
But I have to do this.

29:44.040 --> 29:45.560
I have to do it.

29:48.360 --> 29:50.600
John wants me to do it, Linda.

29:54.680 --> 29:55.760
My brother.

29:58.640 --> 30:00.200
And I'm gonna do it.

30:48.200 --> 30:49.800
Was it fear or was it hatred?

30:51.760 --> 30:53.240
Was what fear or hatred?

30:54.520 --> 30:55.520
Isiah.

31:02.960 --> 31:05.280
You had a one-way ticket to Glasgow
in your pocket.

31:10.000 --> 31:12.000
Your wife and kids left
three days ago.

31:13.680 --> 31:16.320
Now I'm gonna ask you again.

31:19.680 --> 31:24.280
Was it fear of the Italians
or hatred of us

31:24.360 --> 31:27.680
that made you unlock the door
and give up my brother?

31:28.280 --> 31:30.040
I didn't unlock any door.

31:34.760 --> 31:35.880
Here, have a drink.

31:37.760 --> 31:38.840
You're gonna need it.

31:42.920 --> 31:46.320
35 Drumcree Street Parkhead, Glasgow.

31:46.440 --> 31:49.040
Please, please, please, please...

31:50.000 --> 31:53.240
We have allegiances
with Catholic gangs in that city.

31:53.320 --> 31:56.360
Your family are safe
only at my discretion.

31:57.400 --> 32:00.560
Now explain to me

32:01.600 --> 32:04.000
why you were catching
a midnight train to Glasgow.

32:05.680 --> 32:06.840
You mean you don't know?

32:08.880 --> 32:11.880
I run a factory full of black leg
non union labor.

32:12.880 --> 32:16.200
I live in a street full of men
laid off or on strike.

32:17.640 --> 32:19.240
Look at the photograph, Mr. Devlin,

32:19.320 --> 32:21.240
and tell me who are the men
that contacted you.

32:21.320 --> 32:23.000
No. No, you listen to me.

32:23.080 --> 32:24.080
[clears throat]

32:24.160 --> 32:28.240
I get spat at, windows smashed,
petrol on the curtains.

32:28.320 --> 32:32.080
But for fear of you,
I clock in every fucking morning.

32:32.160 --> 32:35.520
And today, two men are shot
and burnt on my shift.

32:35.600 --> 32:38.280
And you ask me why I'm getting
on the midnight train to Glasgow?

32:48.280 --> 32:49.840
Who else has keys to that door?

32:50.880 --> 32:52.960
They hang on a hook inside my office.

32:54.560 --> 32:56.680
Today I left the office unlocked.

32:56.760 --> 32:58.360
-Why?
-Because I forgot.

32:59.040 --> 33:00.320
Because I left in a hurry.

33:00.400 --> 33:02.920
Because there were men
trying to set fire to the factory.

33:05.200 --> 33:08.160
Mr. Shelby, may I tell you something?

33:10.240 --> 33:11.800
You have a lot of enemies.

33:13.280 --> 33:16.280
Communists. Italians.

33:20.560 --> 33:22.560
Before the factory came out on strike,

33:22.640 --> 33:26.200
I heard word
that two Italians attended

33:26.280 --> 33:28.440
a communist party meeting
in Stechford.

33:29.120 --> 33:30.640
They hardly spoke English.

33:31.840 --> 33:35.360
Now, if they got a party man
into the factory,

33:35.440 --> 33:37.840
it might have been him
that unlocked the door for them.

33:41.960 --> 33:43.160
Mr. Shelby...

33:44.600 --> 33:47.760
My train leaves at 12:00.
It's just gone 11:00.

33:47.880 --> 33:49.200
I can still make it.

33:51.640 --> 33:52.920
Please.

33:53.840 --> 33:54.840
For my kids.

34:02.120 --> 34:03.720
I need you here.

34:03.800 --> 34:07.040
Isiah? Get three of our men
with police badges

34:07.120 --> 34:08.920
to watch Mr. Devlin's house.

34:09.000 --> 34:10.600
[Devlin] Mr. Shelby, please...

34:13.480 --> 34:15.639
Our friends in Glasgow
will take care of your family.

34:18.159 --> 34:19.320
For the curtains.

34:21.560 --> 34:25.159
Before you,
I was an ordinary working man.

34:25.560 --> 34:27.600
Yeah, and now you're one of us.

34:40.440 --> 34:41.639
[door closes]

34:49.040 --> 34:50.360
[music playing]

34:59.520 --> 35:04.840
♪ Blackbird, blackbird
Singing the blues all day ♪

35:04.920 --> 35:08.200
♪ Right outside of my door ♪

35:27.880 --> 35:29.160
[music stops playing]

35:31.920 --> 35:34.280
-Who is it?
-It's Tommy Shelby.

35:39.400 --> 35:41.560
-Is this union business?
-Yes.

35:41.640 --> 35:44.000
So conduct it in the proper place
at the proper time.

35:44.920 --> 35:46.400
I've come to make an improved offer.

35:59.440 --> 36:00.560
I heard music.

36:02.000 --> 36:03.480
What's your improved offer?

36:04.520 --> 36:06.560
-Do I not get a drink?
-No.

36:14.400 --> 36:16.760
Have you ever seen any of the men
in this photograph before?

36:18.000 --> 36:19.000
What?

36:24.080 --> 36:26.840
You're a member
of the Stechford Communist party.

36:27.640 --> 36:30.800
I'm told two Italian men
attended a meeting recently.

36:30.880 --> 36:33.520
Did you see either of the men
in this picture?

36:38.280 --> 36:40.680
As the Small Heath coordinator

36:40.760 --> 36:42.920
for the Organisation
of the Maintenance of Supplies,

36:43.000 --> 36:45.120
I have also been sworn in
as a Special...

36:45.200 --> 36:46.360
[scoffs]

36:47.520 --> 36:51.160
We have reason to believe
that outside agitators from overseas

36:51.240 --> 36:54.240
are attempting to foment trouble
in our factories

36:54.320 --> 36:58.520
in advance of a General Strike
which could take place at any moment.

36:58.600 --> 37:00.400
It's a matter of national security.

37:01.720 --> 37:03.040
May I look at your badge?

37:04.800 --> 37:05.800
Yes.

37:08.400 --> 37:09.560
[clears throat]

37:17.160 --> 37:18.800
What would you
like to drink, Constable?

37:18.880 --> 37:20.880
Whiskey. I'm actually a sergeant.

37:22.040 --> 37:23.600
I only have beer. Times are hard.

37:24.640 --> 37:27.240
How long has it been since you've had
a bottle of M&amp;B bitter?

37:28.360 --> 37:29.360
Help yourself.

37:33.560 --> 37:34.560
Have a seat.

37:42.160 --> 37:45.680
You know, when this business began,
I did some research on you.

37:46.680 --> 37:49.280
It turns out I know someone
who used to know you very well.

37:50.560 --> 37:51.800
Kitty Jurossi.

37:56.440 --> 37:59.640
You were in love with Kitty's sister,
Greta Jurossi. Before the war.

37:59.720 --> 38:01.400
Do you remember Greta Jurossi?

38:03.440 --> 38:04.960
Her parents were Italian.

38:05.800 --> 38:07.880
They didn't approve of
a Watery Lane Gypsy.

38:07.960 --> 38:12.320
But you won them over.
With your charm. Sweetness.

38:15.240 --> 38:19.000
Very, very thorough research.

38:19.480 --> 38:22.840
Greta died at the age of 19.
Of consumption.

38:25.000 --> 38:28.760
And Kitty said you were
at her bedside for three months.

38:28.840 --> 38:30.640
Every day. Holding her hand.

38:32.200 --> 38:34.280
And after she died,
you went away to war.

38:36.560 --> 38:39.560
Kitty said that the sweet boy
who left never came back.

38:39.640 --> 38:41.080
No one came back.

38:42.600 --> 38:44.080
Here's the funniest thing.

38:45.720 --> 38:48.080
She said in those days
you believed in things.

38:48.600 --> 38:50.840
Justice. Fairness.

38:51.840 --> 38:54.240
Once you saw a man beating
his horse and you fought him.

38:54.320 --> 38:55.920
He was twice your size
but you beat him.

38:56.000 --> 38:57.720
And then you beat him
with his own whip.

39:00.000 --> 39:02.240
Kitty always liked to tell tall tales.

39:03.200 --> 39:04.800
She's a party member now.

39:06.280 --> 39:08.400
She swears before you
enlisted in the army,

39:08.480 --> 39:10.280
you joined
the communist party yourself.

39:11.200 --> 39:12.520
[sighs]

39:12.600 --> 39:13.600
[clears throat]

39:14.640 --> 39:15.880
Is that true?

39:22.280 --> 39:24.120
[music plays]

39:26.560 --> 39:30.840
When I was at the door
I saw you through the curtains.

39:32.360 --> 39:33.680
You were dancing alone.

39:37.440 --> 39:39.480
I've also done my research.

39:45.640 --> 39:48.280
Your sweetheart was at Passchendaele,

39:49.800 --> 39:52.920
when he came back he was listed
among the shell shocked.

39:54.480 --> 39:56.360
Blew his own fucking brains out.

40:05.600 --> 40:06.920
I don't know any men in the photo.

40:11.720 --> 40:12.720
You haven't looked.

40:14.600 --> 40:16.960
This afternoon two men
came into my factory

40:17.040 --> 40:18.760
and tried to kill my brother.

40:18.840 --> 40:21.560
I believe a Stechford
communist party member let him in.

40:22.240 --> 40:25.440
I was wondering if you might be able
to help me in my investigations.

40:32.200 --> 40:33.640
Kitty said next time I see you,

40:33.720 --> 40:35.520
before we start fighting,

40:36.400 --> 40:38.600
I should send you her love
from the good old days...

40:39.840 --> 40:40.920
And give you this.

40:43.520 --> 40:47.520
Greta Jurossi and Tommy Shelby
in Blackpool.

40:57.480 --> 40:59.240
Do you recognize the boy
in the photograph?

41:23.320 --> 41:24.520
I'll leave that here.

41:29.080 --> 41:31.040
Apologies for interrupting your dance.

41:36.240 --> 41:37.240
[door opens]

41:39.640 --> 41:40.640
[door closes]

42:22.400 --> 42:23.400
[sighs]

42:29.160 --> 42:30.400
[sniffles]

42:30.480 --> 42:31.520
[exhales sharply] Fuck.

42:33.520 --> 42:34.600
[door opens]

42:53.920 --> 42:55.040
Arthur...

42:56.000 --> 42:57.400
I need you to listen to me.

42:59.720 --> 43:01.640
I need you to listen to me, Arthur.

43:05.720 --> 43:07.480
The world is changing.

43:10.320 --> 43:12.080
Listen to me, Arthur.

43:14.400 --> 43:17.520
Listen to the sweet voice of Jesus...

43:59.840 --> 44:00.960
[exhales slowly]

44:14.400 --> 44:15.400
[gunshot]

44:17.960 --> 44:19.760
-Finn?
-It came from Arthur's house.

44:22.720 --> 44:23.720
Arthur!

44:26.120 --> 44:27.120
Arthur!

44:27.920 --> 44:28.920
Where is he?

44:31.240 --> 44:32.240
Arthur?

44:33.440 --> 44:34.680
He fired the bullet.

44:38.280 --> 44:43.680
Linda says it's the modern way, Tom.

44:44.000 --> 44:45.200
[sniffles]

44:47.280 --> 44:48.600
It's the modern way.

44:49.040 --> 44:50.800
Yeah. Yeah.

44:51.600 --> 44:53.080
Yeah. It's all right.

44:53.160 --> 44:54.160
[sniffles]

44:55.560 --> 44:56.760
It's all right, brother.

45:03.280 --> 45:04.400
You did well.

45:04.480 --> 45:06.280
God spoke to him, not me.

45:17.040 --> 45:18.160
[sighs]

45:31.760 --> 45:33.240
[Polly] What are you doing here?

45:33.320 --> 45:35.360
On Mondays, I do the inventory.

45:35.440 --> 45:37.400
Make sure nobody's dipping their hand.

45:38.600 --> 45:41.000
Well, it's my job now.

45:42.360 --> 45:43.600
I'm back.

45:43.680 --> 45:46.520
And there's gonna be nobody dipping
their hand with me here,

45:46.600 --> 45:48.520
not unless they want it cut off.

45:49.040 --> 45:50.040
[door closes]

46:00.000 --> 46:02.000
[Linda] I said to Arthur while
I'm in this fucking place

46:02.080 --> 46:03.720
I want something to keep my mind busy.

46:04.200 --> 46:05.800
What? You're going to take bets?

46:05.880 --> 46:09.000
I've always been able to do addition
and subtraction without pen and paper.

46:09.800 --> 46:11.240
But I'll need a telephone.

46:12.120 --> 46:15.040
Apparently we have special clients
who take bets by telephone.

46:15.120 --> 46:16.520
Linda?

46:18.440 --> 46:19.920
This is a betting shop.

46:20.560 --> 46:21.560
Look.

46:22.240 --> 46:24.440
Arthur said yes. Tommy said yes.

46:24.520 --> 46:27.120
But did God say yes?
Gambling is a sin, Linda.

46:27.200 --> 46:29.040
It's not me that's doing the gambling.

46:29.880 --> 46:31.080
I'm just taking the bets.

46:36.400 --> 46:37.400
[door opens]

46:39.440 --> 46:40.440
[door closes]

46:41.440 --> 46:44.400
The rule is that door should
always remain locked until 9:00 a.m.

46:47.320 --> 46:50.280
Right. Boy. Boy, where are you going?

46:51.080 --> 46:53.840
Well, Arthur's not coming in today.
He's taking the day off. So...

46:54.240 --> 46:55.240
"So" what?

46:55.840 --> 46:58.360
So, today, Tommy said
that I'm in charge.

46:58.920 --> 47:00.480
Sorry, you're in charge?

47:02.160 --> 47:03.400
Yeah. That's what he said.

47:08.320 --> 47:10.000
All right, sweetheart.

47:13.720 --> 47:14.960
Ladies?

47:15.040 --> 47:20.240
Let's give our boss a first day
that he'll never forget.

47:28.920 --> 47:29.920
[door opens]

47:30.600 --> 47:32.560
Sending Finn to the shop
was a mistake.

47:32.640 --> 47:34.120
They've already found out
he's a virgin

47:34.200 --> 47:37.560
and are arranging a girl
for him this afternoon.

47:37.640 --> 47:38.760
I thought Linda was there.

47:39.560 --> 47:41.640
She is. She loved the idea.

47:41.840 --> 47:44.680
-[scoffs]
-Yeah, I know. She even swears now.

47:44.960 --> 47:47.640
"Fuck." Sounds funny coming from her.

47:47.720 --> 47:49.800
Polly says in the end
we all turn into our mother.

47:50.640 --> 47:52.400
Ah, well... Keep an eye on her.

47:52.680 --> 47:53.680
Hmm.

47:54.800 --> 47:56.880
The whore watching the Madonna.

47:57.960 --> 47:59.560
Does Finn know what they have planned?

47:59.640 --> 48:02.600
-No.
-Do they have someone?

48:03.040 --> 48:05.920
Yes. A girl I used to work with.

48:08.320 --> 48:11.680
-Is she nice?
-No. She's from Aston.

48:12.240 --> 48:14.040
They're paying her out of petty cash.

48:14.120 --> 48:15.600
Right, well, call 'em,

48:16.560 --> 48:18.040
and tell them to pay extra

48:19.000 --> 48:20.240
and get someone nice.

48:21.160 --> 48:22.880
Nice women don't do
that sort of thing.

48:23.320 --> 48:25.480
Yes, they do. What about you?

48:28.480 --> 48:31.000
I mean in the past. Come on.

48:31.640 --> 48:33.040
Where are we going?

48:33.120 --> 48:35.440
Somewhere I’ve not been
in a long time.

48:39.440 --> 48:41.640
[birds chirping]

48:54.280 --> 48:56.120
Are we expecting somebody?

48:59.680 --> 49:01.600
Tommy, I'm fucking freezing here.

49:04.560 --> 49:05.800
We used to come here.

49:08.600 --> 49:12.560
She'd wait for hours for me,
when I couldn't make it.

49:14.280 --> 49:18.240
And I'd wait for her
when her family kept her in.

49:20.520 --> 49:21.520
Who?

49:23.800 --> 49:24.880
Some girl.

49:26.160 --> 49:28.040
Some girl before France.

49:33.840 --> 49:35.360
I've not been back here since.

49:41.800 --> 49:43.440
Wanted to come here with you.

49:56.280 --> 49:57.920
Are you kissing her or me?

50:00.640 --> 50:01.720
You.

50:48.240 --> 50:51.200
I want Shelby Company Limited
to increase

50:51.280 --> 50:54.760
non-taxable charitable contributions
to local charities

50:54.840 --> 50:57.120
by 25% as of now.

50:58.800 --> 51:03.120
I'm gonna build two new institutes
for destitute children.

51:03.200 --> 51:05.520
One in Saltley, one in Digbeth.

51:06.200 --> 51:08.040
I have already identified
the buildings.

51:08.120 --> 51:09.920
Two former workhouses.

51:11.720 --> 51:13.960
I want you to be in charge
of the project.

51:16.520 --> 51:17.920
Right, come on, let's go.

51:18.000 --> 51:19.040
Why?

51:27.400 --> 51:29.600
Because I promised someone
I'd change the world.

51:34.160 --> 51:36.680
You do realize, Tommy,
we're all going fucking mad here.

51:38.240 --> 51:39.240
Yeah, I know.

51:40.520 --> 51:41.520
Come on.

51:47.360 --> 51:48.920
[footsteps approaching]

51:53.920 --> 51:54.920
Finn?

51:55.800 --> 51:56.960
Come here.

52:00.720 --> 52:02.280
How was your day?

52:02.360 --> 52:03.640
Yeah, it was okay.

52:05.000 --> 52:07.680
Good man. Well done. No trouble?

52:08.640 --> 52:10.600
No. No trouble.

52:13.000 --> 52:14.120
And she looked after you?

52:16.880 --> 52:18.080
[sighs]

52:19.920 --> 52:21.720
I don't want it like that
ever again, Tom.

52:22.800 --> 52:25.960
Not when they don't even
want to do it, except for the money.

52:26.760 --> 52:28.600
Everything's for the money, Finn.

52:28.680 --> 52:30.240
Yeah, I know. But...

52:33.440 --> 52:34.680
She said, "Be a man."

52:36.800 --> 52:37.800
And were you a man?

52:39.120 --> 52:40.120
Yeah.

52:41.840 --> 52:45.440
But then I apologized to her,
'cause she just looked so tired.

52:49.280 --> 52:50.280
Sit down, Finn.

52:53.560 --> 52:55.080
[clears throat]

52:55.320 --> 52:58.920
Right, listen to me, Finn,
she was right.

53:00.000 --> 53:01.600
You need to be a fucking man.

53:02.440 --> 53:04.280
People get tired.

53:04.360 --> 53:07.200
Working in a fucking factory
gets you tired.

53:07.680 --> 53:09.800
I don't go round apologizing. Do I?

53:10.080 --> 53:11.080
No.

53:11.160 --> 53:15.120
There's an empty space here
to be filled. You understand?

53:16.080 --> 53:19.080
-Yeah.
-So, be a fucking man.

53:21.800 --> 53:23.000
Okay, Tom.

53:37.320 --> 53:38.920
[jazz band playing]

53:49.840 --> 53:51.640
[indistinct conversations]

54:07.560 --> 54:09.560
-Champagne, please.
-Of course.

54:11.280 --> 54:12.280
Madam,

54:13.160 --> 54:16.320
women alone are not allowed
at the bar.

54:16.960 --> 54:18.360
Will someone be joining you?

54:19.400 --> 54:20.600
What do you think?

54:55.880 --> 54:57.800
-[music stops]
-[applause]

54:59.400 --> 55:00.600
[drinks pouring]

55:02.880 --> 55:04.080
[grunts softly]

55:06.560 --> 55:08.680
This is public enough, no?

55:09.560 --> 55:10.560
Yes.

55:14.360 --> 55:15.360
So?

55:17.000 --> 55:19.560
The boy in the hospital
is out of bounds.

55:19.640 --> 55:21.880
And I will ask you to spare
Finn and Arthur.

55:24.920 --> 55:26.800
In return for what?

55:32.120 --> 55:33.400
Tommy Shelby.

55:39.360 --> 55:42.240
And why should I trust you?

55:44.280 --> 55:46.000
Because you know our history.

55:48.440 --> 55:50.320
You know what happened between us.

55:53.240 --> 55:55.520
You are an unlikely Cassius.

55:57.560 --> 55:58.560
Hmm.

56:03.000 --> 56:05.960
You know, my mother...

56:07.680 --> 56:09.560
My mother knew your mother.

56:11.880 --> 56:13.400
She taught her how to read.

56:16.000 --> 56:19.040
Did she tell you that John
and Arthur spared her life?

56:19.120 --> 56:21.640
-When Tommy wanted her dead.
-Yeah.

56:23.440 --> 56:26.840
And now she's giving me
the information about you people.

56:28.240 --> 56:30.040
So Tommy Shelby was right.

56:33.640 --> 56:39.200
His ruthlessness was justified.

56:41.280 --> 56:44.000
You should have killed her
when you had the chance.

56:46.360 --> 56:47.960
John was a good boy.

56:51.960 --> 56:53.200
Arthur tries.

56:55.440 --> 56:56.600
Tommy's different.

56:58.440 --> 57:01.600
You take Tommy. Spare the rest.

57:06.720 --> 57:07.720
You know,

57:09.400 --> 57:11.920
my mother used to say this about you.

57:13.680 --> 57:16.160
She said, "That Polly Gray,

57:17.440 --> 57:20.800
that child would never
let go of a grievance."

57:20.880 --> 57:22.160
[chuckles]

57:24.960 --> 57:27.080
And she loves to dance.

57:31.240 --> 57:33.160
What do you say? Hmm?

57:34.200 --> 57:35.680
You wanna dance?

57:42.200 --> 57:44.040
I don't dance anymore.

57:45.800 --> 57:47.760
Yeah, that's a shame.

57:55.000 --> 57:57.320
'Cause you're dancing with me.

58:20.040 --> 58:22.360
♪ On a gathering storm comes ♪

58:22.440 --> 58:23.840
♪ A tall handsome man ♪

58:23.920 --> 58:26.400
♪ In a dusty black coat with ♪

58:26.480 --> 58:28.200
♪ A red right hand ♪
